AB  - The proceedings contain 26 papers. The special focus in this conference is on the study and modelling of environmental health risk problems. The topics include: vegetation fires and release of radioactivity into the air; assessment of diesel particulate matter exposure among underground mine workers; an investigation into the association of ozone with traffic-related air pollutants using a quantile regression approach; a choice experiment approach to the valuation of air pollution in Mashhad, Iran; multiscale comparison of air quality modeling for an ozone occurrence during the 1996 Paso Del Norte Ozone Campaign; generic mapping of human activity-based exposure scenarios to petroleum hydrocarbon contaminants in an oil producing area of the Niger Delta region of Nigeria; modeling vapor intrusion processes and evaluating risks using subslab data; assessment of fungal contamination in a Portuguese maternity unit; respiratory toxicity of Aspergillus versicolor in Slovakia; environmental health issues in the wake of a major earthquake in West Sumatra, Indonesia; cell-based bioassay for compounds with prooxidant activity; synthetic musks fragrances in the aquatic environment; evaluation of QMRA performance for Listeria monocytogenes in cold smoked salmon; study of mutagenic effects of a packaging system with oxygen absorbers on sweet bakery products; work conditions and occupational morbidity in Latvia; eco-biosociocultural H5N1 disease model in Egypt; groundwater quality on a waste disposal area due to sand mining activities in Sao Paulo State, Brazil; and ecological effects of underwater destruction of detonators in Lake Ormtjarn, Sweden.
